---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AuthorReviewerCard from '@/components/editorial/AuthorReviewerCard.astro';
import ContextualLinks from '@/components/seo/ContextualLinks.astro';
import { StructuredDataGenerator } from '@/lib/seo';
import { AuthorManager } from '@/lib/editorial';

const siteUrl = 'https://lic-calculators.com';
const author = AuthorManager.getDefaultAuthor();
const reviewer = AuthorManager.getDefaultReviewer();

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Educational Guides', url: '/guides' },
  { name: 'Paid-Up vs Surrender', url: '/guides/lic-paid-up-vs-surrender' }
];

const articleSchema = StructuredDataGenerator.generateArticle({
  headline: 'LIC Paid-Up vs. Surrender: Which Option is Financially Better?',
  description: 'Comparing the financial trade-offs between converting an LIC policy into a reduced Paid-Up policy versus taking an immediate cash Surrender payout.',
  url: `${siteUrl}/guides/lic-paid-up-vs-surrender`,
  publishedDate: '2026-01-08T00:00:00Z',
  modifiedDate: '2026-01-20T00:00:00Z',
  author,
  reviewer
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LIC Paid-Up vs Surrender: Which Option is Financially Better?"
  description="Comparing the financial trade-offs between converting an LIC policy into a reduced Paid-Up policy versus taking an immediate cash Surrender payout."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-10">
    <div class="space-y-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-8">
      <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-700 border border-indigo-200">
        Decision Guide • Financial Comparison
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        LIC Paid-Up Policy vs. Cash Surrender: Which is Better?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        If you are struggling to continue paying your annual LIC premiums, you have two primary options: convert your policy to Paid-Up or Surrender it for immediate cash. Here is the mathematical comparison.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Tool CTA -->
    <div class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-200 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-indigo-900">Run a side-by-side numerical comparison</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-indigo-700">See exact numerical projections for Surrender Now vs. Paid-Up on your policy.</p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="/lic-surrender-analysis"
        class="px-4 py-2 bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white font-bold text-xs rounded-xl transition-colors shrink-0 shadow-sm"
      >
        Run Decision Analysis &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6 text-slate-700">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. What is a Paid-Up Policy?</h2>
      <p>
        When you stop paying premiums on an active policy after paying for at least 2 full years, your policy does not terminate. Instead, it automatically converts to a <strong>Paid-Up policy</strong>. The Sum Assured is reduced in proportion to the number of premiums paid:
      </p>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">
        Paid-Up Sum Assured = (Number of Premiums Paid / Total Premiums Payable) * Original Sum Assured
      </div>
      <p>
        The reduced amount is paid to you at the original maturity date, or to your nominee in the event of death during the term.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Comparison: Paid-Up vs. Cash Surrender</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-xs text-left border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 font-bold border-b border-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3">Feature</th>
              <th class="p-3">Cash Surrender</th>
              <th class="p-3">Convert to Paid-Up</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-600">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-800">Timing of Payout</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-emerald-700 font-semibold">Immediate cash into bank</td>
              <td class="p-3">At end of policy term (or death)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-800">Capital Shortfall</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-rose-700 font-semibold">High (35% to 60% loss)</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-emerald-700 font-semibold">Zero capital forfeiture</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-800">Life Cover</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-rose-700">Terminates immediately</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-emerald-700">Remains active for Paid-Up amount</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Expert Actuarial Recommendation</h2>
      <p>
        Unless you are facing an acute emergency requiring immediate liquidity, <strong>converting to a Paid-Up policy is almost always mathematically superior to immediate cash surrender</strong> because it preserves your deposited principal and maintains life cover until maturity.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Links -->
    <ContextualLinks currentPath="/lic-surrender-value-calculator" />

    <!-- Author Card -->
    <AuthorReviewerCard author={author} reviewer={reviewer} lastReviewedDate="January 2026" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
